  "checks": {
    "identity-and-scale": "All eight native poses retain the bald broad Laborer, two brass-tipped brown braids, cream rolled sleeves, leather waistcoat and boots. One original common raster scale is preserved. The calibrated source root follows fixed toolbox features, not changing chip-pile silhouette; this is a kneeling local sequence, not standing or gait calibration.",
    "station-and-foot-contact": "Reviewed the complete kneeling0-7, visible bent knees and boot positions as he reaches and returns the broom. Fixed toolbox registration replaces the unreliable moving-pile anchor. Fresh residual0.465px with remaining bounded corrections at most1px. Whole authored cell boundaries exclude neighboring fragments and retain each complete pose and detached props. Translating sole contacts are excluded.",
    "hand-and-tool-contact": "Right hand holds the same short wooden broom throughout approach0/1, push2/3/4, lift5/6 and return7. Left hand shifts toward the broom during the forward reach and withdraws on return; all visible wrists are connected. No tool appears without a hand or transfers to a new owner.",
    "prop-continuity": "One identical iron-bound toolbox and its handle/contents remain fixed beside the knee. Chips collect into the swept pile and remain visible at7; no claim of resource removal or repeated delivery. Toolbox panels are not warped or animated. Chip fragments belonging to adjacent cells are excluded by documented source-cell ownership.",
    "completion-and-reset": "Controlled gallery playback must expose all authored holds0-7, finish once at7, retain the final pose for sustained time and restart only on explicit task reset. No seamless7-to0 approval, economic output, standing-body placement or live activation is implied."
